ubturbo (1.0.0-9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Align Debian packaging with RPM spec 1.0.0-9
  * Add ubturbo-smap and ubturbo-ucache binary packages to mirror the
    RPM sub-packages defined in ubturbo.spec. The ubdma sub-package is
    intentionally not built (its kernel module is not shipped).
  * Build all components (smap, ucache, rmrs, devel) from debian/rules
    instead of rmrs alone.
  * Lintian cleanup:
    - Add Rules-Requires-Root: binary-targets to the source stanza.
    - Stop polluting the build host's /usr/lib64 during build; provide
      libboundscheck via the multiarch symlink inside DESTDIR only.
    - Remove redundant manual patch application from rules; rely on the
      3.0 (quilt) source format to apply debian/patches/series.
    - Replace fragile "mv ../*.deb ../../" in build-deb.sh with
      deterministic artifact handling.
    - Tighten maintainer-script permissions and sudoers handling.

 -- openEuler Maintainers <maintainers@openeuler.org>  Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0800

ubturbo (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging based on RPM spec 1.0.0-5
  * Add pre-migration remote available numa detection

